.TH SDL_CloseAudioDevice 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CloseAudioDevice \- Close a previously-opened audio device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_CloseAudioDevice(SDL_AudioDeviceID devid);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The application should close open audio devices once they are no longer needed\[char46]
.PP
This function may block briefly while pending audio data is played by the hardware, so that applications don\(aqt drop the last buffer of data they supplied if terminating immediately afterwards\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I devid
an audio device id previously returned by
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice ()\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice (3)
